 //   * Pause the link after `idleTicksBeforePause` consecutive idle ticks, so a terminal at
 //     rest costs nothing. 8 ticks (67ms at 120Hz, 133ms at 60Hz) is longer than the gap of
 //     a 30fps producer at either rate, so a steady stream never pause/resume-churns.
+//   * LOCAL PATCH 0016: a producer SLOWER than that window (a 12 Hz agent spinner at 120 or
+//     144 Hz: an 83ms gap against a 56-67ms window) churns anyway, once per frame, and the
+//     8 idle ticks before each pause bought nothing. Each tick is a synchronous CoreAnimation
+//     round trip into WindowServer (SLSDisplayStatusQuery), and a 12 Hz spinner at 144 Hz
+//     spent 9 ticks per paint. So when the gap since the previous paint already exceeded the
+//     window, the link pauses after ONE idle tick instead. It can only pause where the old
+//     rule was going to pause anyway (plus at most one extra resume when a slow producer
+//     speeds up), so a steady 30-60fps stream is untouched. Measured: 2160 -> 480 ticks for
+//     240 spinner paints at 144 Hz; 60/30fps streams unchanged (.afk/research/
+//     metal-idle-encode-2026-10-18.md). `SWIFTTERM_ADAPTIVE_PAUSE=0` restores the fixed
+//     window, and is how check-display-link.sh case 9 falsifies itself.
